hadiths[82]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1523","'Sayyiduna Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Glorified and Exalted be He, chose Kinana from among the descendants of Sayyiduna Isma’il (peace be upon him), and chose Quraysh from among Kinana, and chose Banu Hashim from among Quraysh, and chose me from among Banu Hashim.'"
"1524","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: On the Day of Resurrection, I will be the leader of the children of Adam. And my grave will be the first to be opened, and I will be the first to intercede, and my intercession will be the first to be accepted."
"1525","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: The example of what Allah has sent me with of guidance and knowledge is like rain that falls upon the earth. Some of it is a portion that absorbs the water and brings forth much grass and greenery. Another portion is hard and holds the water, so Allah benefits the people with it; they drink from it, give drink to others, and graze their animals. And another portion is barren land that neither retains water nor grows grass (like a smooth rock upon which water falls and flows away). This is the example of the one who understands Allah’s religion and benefits from what Allah has sent me with; he learns and teaches others. And the example of the one who does not pay attention and does not accept the guidance with which I have been sent by Allah."
"1526","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: My example and the example of my religion with which Allah has sent me is like the example of a person who came to his people and said, ""O my people! I have seen the army with my own eyes (i.e., the enemy's army), and I am a clear warner, so flee quickly."" Now, some people from his nation accepted his word and fled that very evening and went away safely, while some denied him and remained at their place till morning. In the morning, the army attacked them and destroyed them and uprooted them completely. Thus, this is the example of the one who obeyed me and followed what I have brought, and the one who did not listen to me and denied the true religion."
"1527","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My example and the example of the other prophets who came before me is like that of a person who built a house and adorned and beautified it, but left a space for one brick in one of its corners. So people began to walk around it and admired the building, and they said: Why was this one brick not placed here? The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am that brick, and I am the Seal of the Prophets."
"1528","Narrated Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I know a stone in Mecca which used to greet me before I was commissioned with Prophethood. I still recognize it now."
"1529","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions were at the place of Zawra { اور زوراء مدینہ میں مسجد اور بازار کے نزدیک ایک مقام ہے } The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for a bowl of water and placed his hand in it, then water began to gush forth from between his fingers and all the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) performed ablution with it. Qatadah said: I asked Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), ""O Abu Hamzah! How many people were you at that time?"" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""About three hundred."""
"1530","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the year of the Battle of Tabuk. During this journey, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would combine two prayers. Thus, he would combine and perform Zuhr and Asr together, and Maghrib and Isha together. One day, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) delayed the prayer. Then he came out and combined and performed Zuhr and Asr together, then went inside. After that, he came out again and combined and performed Maghrib and Isha together. After this, he said: ""Tomorrow, if Allah wills, you will reach the spring of Tabuk, and you will not reach it before sunrise. Whoever among you reaches the spring, let him not touch its water until I arrive."" Sayyiduna Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then we reached the spring, and two men had reached there before us. The condition of the spring's water was such that it was as much as a shoelace, and that too was trickling slowly. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked those two men, ""Did you touch its water?"" They said, ""Yes."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) rebuked them (because they had acted against his instruction) and conveyed to them what Allah had willed. Then the people collected a little water in a vessel with their hands. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) washed his hands and face in it, then poured that water into the spring. The spring began to gush forth and flow, and the people (gave water to their animals and themselves). After this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Mu'adh! If you live long, you will see that the water of this (spring) will fill gardens."" (This too was a great miracle of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). There were thirty thousand men in that army, and in another narration, it is said there were seventy thousand men.)"
"1531","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and asked him for food. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave him half a wasq of barley (a wasq is sixty sa’). Then that man, his wife, and his guest kept eating from it, until the man measured it. Then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If you had not measured it, you would have continued to eat from it and it would have remained as it was (because by measuring it, their trust in Allah was lost and impatience was shown, so the blessing was gone)."
"1532","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): When the trench was being dug (around Madinah), I found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) hungry. I returned to my wife and said, ""Do you have anything (to eat)? For I have found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) extremely hungry."" She brought out a bag in which there was a sa’ (measure) of barley, and we had a young goat at home. I slaughtered it, and my wife ground the flour. She finished at the same time as I did, and I cut the meat and put it in the pot. Then, as I was about to return to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), my wife said, ""Do not disgrace me before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and those with him (because the food is little, so do not invite too many people)."" I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and quietly said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I have slaughtered a young goat and prepared a sa’ of barley flour that we had. Please come with a few people."" Upon hearing this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called out, ""O people of the trench! Jabir has prepared a feast for you, so come!"" And he said, ""Do not take the pot off the fire, and do not bake the bread until I come."" Then I went home, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also arrived. He was in front, and the people were behind him. I went to my wife, and she said, ""You will be in trouble, and people will blame you."" I said, ""I only did what you told me (but the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, announced it and invited everyone)."" I brought out the flour, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) put his blessed lips on it and prayed for blessing. Then he went to our pot, spat in it, and prayed for blessing. After that, he said (to my wife), ""Call a woman who can bake bread with you, and keep taking out from the pot with a ladle, but do not take it off the fire."" Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: There were a thousand men with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I swear, all of them ate until they were satisfied and left, and the pot was still boiling as it was, and the flour was the same, and bread was still being made from it."
"1533","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were one hundred and thirty men with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Does anyone have any food?"" A man produced a sa’ of grain, or a little less or more. Then all of it was kneaded. Then a polytheist came, his hair disheveled, driving some goats, and he reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Are you selling (the goat) or giving it as a gift?"" He said, ""No, I am selling it."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) bought a goat from him, and its meat was prepared, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered its liver to be roasted. The narrator said: By Allah, there was not a single one among those one hundred and thirty men for whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not separate some of that liver; if he was present, he gave it to him, and if he was not present, he set aside his share. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) took out meat in two bowls, then all of us ate from them and were satisfied, and in fact, some was left in the bowls, which I loaded onto a camel, or he said something similar. (In this hadith, there are two miracles of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): one is the blessing in the liver, and the other is the blessing in the goat.)"
"1534","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the people of Suffa were needy, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once said: ""Whoever has food for two people, let him take a third with him. And whoever has food for four, let him take a fifth or a sixth."" And Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) brought three people, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took ten people (and the family of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was also about ten, so it was as if half the food was for the guests). Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""There was no one in our house except my father and my mother."" The narrator said: ""Perhaps he also mentioned his wife, and a servant who was in the house of mine and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)."" Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) ate the night meal with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then stayed there until the 'Isha prayer was performed. After finishing the prayer, he returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and remained there until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept. After a large part of the night had passed, as much as Allah willed, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came home, and his wife said: 'Where have you been, leaving your guests?' Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'Did you not feed them?' She said: 'The guests did not eat until you came.' She had presented the food to the guests, but the guests did not eat before him."" Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""I hid (out of fear of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr's displeasure), so he called me: 'O lazy, ignorant, or foolish one! May your nose be cut off,' and he spoke harshly to me, and said to the guests: 'Eat, even though this food is not pleasant (because it is untimely).' And Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'By Allah, I will never eat from it.' Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'By Allah, every morsel we picked up, the food below increased, until we were all satisfied, and the food became even more than it was before.' Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) saw that the food was as much as before, or even more, so he said to his wife: 'O sister of Bani Firas (her name was Umm Ruman, and Bani Firas was her tribe), what is this?' She replied: 'By the coolness of my eyes (meaning the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it is even more than before, three times as much.' (This was a miracle of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. From this hadith, it is known that miracles can appear from the friends of Allah.) Then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) ate from it and said: 'The oath I took was from Satan (i.e., out of anger).' Then he took a morsel from it, and after that, he took the food to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I was also there in the morning, and there was a treaty between us and a people (i.e., a pact of peace). When the term of the pact ended, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed twelve men as our leaders, and each had people with him, and Allah knows how many people were with each. Then that food was given to them, and all the people ate from it."
"1535","Sayyiduna Miqdad (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I and my two companions came, and due to hardship (such as hunger, etc.), our eyesight and hearing had weakened. We would present ourselves to the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), but none would accept us. Finally, we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he took us to his house. There were three goats there. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Milk them, all of us will drink, and then we would milk them, and each of us would drink his share and leave the share of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would come at night and greet in such a voice that the sleeping one would not wake, but the awake one would hear. Then he would go to the mosque, pray, then come to his milk and drink it. One night, after I had drunk my share, Satan incited me. Satan said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) goes to the Ansar, they give him gifts, and whatever he needs, he gets. What need does he have for this one sip of milk? Finally, I came and drank that milk. When the milk settled in my stomach and I was sure that now that milk would not be found, then Satan made me regret and said: Woe to you, what have you done? You have drunk the share of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Now when he comes and does not find the milk, he will curse you, and both your world and Hereafter will be ruined. I was wrapped in a sheet; when I covered my feet, my head would be uncovered, and when I covered my head, my feet would be uncovered. I could not sleep, while my companions slept, and they had not done what I had done. Finally, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came, greeted as usual, then went to the mosque and prayed, then came to the milk, opened the vessel, and found nothing in it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head towards the sky. I thought now he will curse, and I am ruined. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Allah! Feed the one who feeds me, and give drink to the one who gives me drink. Hearing this, I tied my sheet tightly, took a knife, and went to the goats to slaughter the fattest one for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I saw that its udder was full of milk. Then I saw that the udders of the other goats were also full of milk. I took a vessel of the household of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in which they did not usually milk (i.e., they did not wish to milk in it). I milked into it until foam rose to the top (so much milk came out), and I brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He said: Did you drink your share of milk at night or not? I said: O Messenger of Allah! Please drink the milk. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) drank and gave it to me. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Drink more. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) drank more, then gave it to me. When I knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was satisfied and I had received his supplication, then I laughed until, out of joy, I fell to the ground. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Miqdad! Did you do something bad? What is it? I said: O Messenger of Allah! This is what happened to me, and I committed this mistake. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The milk of that time (which came down unusually) was Allah’s mercy. Why did you not tell me earlier? We would have awakened our two companions so they could also drink this milk. I said: By Him who sent you with the true word, now I do not care, since you have received Allah’s mercy and I have received it with you, whoever else receives it."
"1536","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that Umm Malik (may Allah be pleased with her) used to send clarified butter (ghee) as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in a small bowl. Then her sons would come and ask for curry from it, and when there was nothing at home, Umm Malik (may Allah be pleased with her) would go to that bowl, and there would be ghee in it. In this way, the curry of her house always remained. Once, Umm Malik (out of eagerness) squeezed out the bowl, and then she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He inquired, ""Did you squeeze it out?"" She replied, ""Yes."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""If you had left it as it was (and taken from it only when needed), it would have always remained."""
"1537","‘Sayyiduna ‘Ubada bin Walid bin ‘Ubada bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I and my father set out towards the tribe of Ansar for the purpose of acquiring knowledge, lest any of their members remain (either they pass away or migrate elsewhere). So, the first person we met was Abu al-Yasar, who was a companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). With him was his slave, who was carrying a bundle of books (letters). Abu al-Yasar was wearing a sheet and a garment called ma’afiri. His slave was also wearing a sheet and a ma’afiri garment (i.e., both master and slave were dressed alike). I said to him, “O uncle, you seem to be upset.” He replied, “So-and-so from the tribe of Banu Haram owed me a debt. I went to his family, greeted them, and asked where he was. They said he was not there. Meanwhile, his young son came out. I asked him, ‘Where is your father?’ He replied, ‘When he heard your voice, he hid in my mother’s hut.’ So I called out and said, ‘O so-and-so! Come out, I know where you are.’ Hearing this, he came out. I said, ‘Why are you hiding from me?’ He replied, ‘By Allah, I will not lie to you. By Allah, I was afraid that I might lie to you or make a promise and then break it, and you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah. By Allah, I am in need.’ I made him swear by Allah, ‘Are you really in need?’ He swore by Allah and said, ‘I am in need.’ I made him swear again, and he swore again. I made him swear a third time, and he swore by Allah again. Then his document or note (debt note) was brought. Abu al-Yasar (may Allah be pleased with him) erased it with his own hand and said, ‘If you get money, pay it; otherwise, you are free.’ So I bear witness, my two eyes saw, and Abu al-Yasar (may Allah be pleased with him) placed his two fingers on his eyes, and my two ears heard, and my heart remembered, and Abu al-Yasar (may Allah be pleased with him) pointed to the vein of his heart (and said): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: Whoever gives respite to a debtor in difficulty or forgives the debt, Allah will keep him under His shade. ‘Ubada said: I said to him, ‘O uncle, if you take your slave’s sheet and give him your ma’afiri garment, then you will both have a complete set of clothes.’ Abu al-Yasar (may Allah be pleased with him) placed his hand on my head and said, ‘O Allah, bless this boy. O my nephew! My two eyes saw, my two ears heard, and my heart remembered,’ and he pointed to the vein of his heart (and said): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: Feed your slave and maidservant what you eat, and clothe them with what you wear. If I give him worldly goods, it is easier for me than that he should take my good deeds on the Day of Resurrection. ‘Ubada (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then we went on until we reached Sayyiduna Jabir bin ‘Abdullah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) in his mosque. He was wrapped in a cloth and was praying. I stepped over people’s necks and sat between him and the qiblah. I said, ‘May Allah have mercy on you, you pray in a single garment while your (other) sheet is lying beside you.’ He gestured to my chest with his hand, spreading his fingers and bending them like a bow, and said, ‘I wanted that a fool like you would come to me, see what I do, and do the same. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to our mosque, and in his hand was a stick of Ibn Tab (a type of date palm). He saw phlegm (spittle) facing the qiblah in the mosque, so he scraped it off with the stick. Then he turned to us and said, “Who among you would like Allah to turn away from him?” We became afraid upon hearing this. Then he said again, “Who among you would like Allah to turn away from him?” We became afraid. Then he said a third time, “Who among you would like Allah to turn away from him?” We said, “O Messenger of Allah! None of us wants that.” He said, “When any of you stands in prayer, Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, is in front of his face (Nawawi said: meaning the direction which Allah has honored, i.e., the Ka‘bah), so do not spit in front of your face, nor to your right, but to your left, under your left foot.” If phlegm comes out quickly, then spit into your garment and fold it over. Then he said, “Bring me perfume.” A young man from our tribe rushed and ran to his house and brought perfume in his palm. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) applied the perfume to the tip of the stick and put it where the phlegm was in the mosque. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: From this hadith, you keep perfume in your mosques. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to the battle of Buwat (which is one of the mountains of Juhaynah). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was searching for Majdi bin ‘Amr al-Juhani (who was a disbeliever), and our situation was such that five, six, or seven men shared one camel, riding it in turns. So, when it was the turn of one Ansari, he made the camel sit, mounted it, then made it stand, but the camel ran off. The Ansari said, “Shay!” (a word used to scold the camel), “May Allah curse you!” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Who is it that curses his camel?” The Ansari said, “It is I, O Messenger of Allah!” He said, “Get down from the camel, for it should not accompany us one upon whom a curse has been invoked. Do not invoke curses upon yourselves, your children, or your wealth, lest it coincide with a time when Allah is asked for something and He grants it (so your curse is accepted and calamity befalls you).” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). When evening came and we reached near a spring of the Arabs, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Who will go ahead of us and fix the pond, drink from it, and give us to drink?” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I stood up and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I am that person.” He said, “And who will go with Jabir?” So Jabbar bin Sakhr stood up. So we both went to the well/spring, drew one or two buckets, then plastered it with mud. After that, we started filling it with water until it was full to the brim. The first to appear to us was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He said, “Do you both permit me (and my animals to drink)?” We said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah!” He let his she-camel loose, it drank, then he pulled its rein, it stopped drinking and urinated. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) took it aside and made it sit. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to the pond, performed ablution from it. I also stood up and performed ablution from the same place where he had performed ablution. Jabbar bin Sakhr (may Allah be pleased with him) went to relieve himself. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up to pray. I had a sheet on my body. I tried to wrap its two ends, but it was short and had loops. Finally, I turned it inside out, then wrapped its two ends, then tied it around my neck, then came and stood to the left of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He took my hand, turned me, and made me stand on his right. Then Jabbar bin Sakhr came, performed ablution, and stood to the left of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) (to pray). He took both our hands and moved us back until he made us stand behind him (it is understood that such an action is permissible in prayer). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) began to stare at me, and I did not know. When I realized, he gestured with his hand to tie my waist (so that my ‘awrah would not be exposed). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) finished the prayer, he said, “O Jabir!” I said, “Here I am, O Messenger of Allah!” He said, “When the sheet is wide, wrap its two ends, and when it is tight, tie it around your waist.” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then we went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and each of us would get one date a day for food, and he would suck it, then chew it with his teeth. We would shake leaves from the trees with our bows and eat them, until (due to heat, dryness, and eating leaves) our mouths became wounded inside. Then one day, the distributor of dates forgot one person. We picked him up and testified that he had not received a date. The distributor gave him a date. He stood up and took the date. Then we went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) until we descended into a wide valley. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went to relieve himself. I followed him with a bucket of water. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) found no cover. He saw two trees at the edge of the valley. He went to one tree, took hold of a branch, and said, “By Allah’s command, follow me.” The tree followed him as a camel with a nose ring follows its leader. Then he went to the other tree, took hold of a branch, and said, “By Allah’s command, follow me.” It also followed him in the same way, until when he reached between the two trees, he joined them together and said, “By Allah’s command, join together before me.” So the two trees joined together. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I ran out, fearing that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) might see me nearby and go farther away. I sat, talking to myself, when suddenly I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) coming from the front, and the two trees had separated and returned to their places. I saw that he stood for a while and gestured with his head to the right and left, then came forward. When he reached me, he said, “O Jabir! Did you see where I stood?” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) replied, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah!” He said, “Go to those two trees and cut a branch from each. When you reach the place where I stood, place one branch on your right and one on your left.” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I stood up, took a stone, broke it, and sharpened it. When it was sharp, I went to the two trees, cut a branch from each, then dragged the branches to the place where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had stood, and placed one branch on the right and one on the left. Then I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, “I have done what you commanded, but what is the reason for it?” He said, “I saw two graves there, and their occupants were being punished, so I wanted to intercede for them. As long as these branches remain fresh, perhaps their punishment will be lessened.” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then we returned to the army. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “O Jabir! Call out for water for ablution.” I called out three times and said, “O Messenger of Allah! There is not a drop of water in the caravan.” There was an Ansari man who used to cool water for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in a water skin that hung from tree branches. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Go to that Ansari and see if there is any water in his water skin.” I went and saw that there was no water in the water skin, only a drop at its mouth, which, if I poured out, the dry water skin would absorb it. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! There is no water in the water skin, only a drop at its mouth, which, if I pour out, the dry water skin would absorb it.” He said, “Go and bring that water skin to me.” I brought the water skin. He took it in his hand, then began to say something I could not understand, and pressed the water skin with his hand. Then he handed it to me and said, “O Jabir! Call for the caravan’s pot (i.e., the large water vessel).” I called out, and it was brought. I placed it before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He passed his hand over the pot, spread his fingers, and placed his hand at its bottom, and said, “O Jabir! Take the water skin and pour it over my hand, saying ‘Bismillah’.” I said ‘Bismillah’ and poured the water. Then I saw water gushing from between his fingers, until the pot boiled and spun and was filled. He said, “O Jabir! Call out to whoever needs water.” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: People came and took water until all were satisfied. I said, “Is there anyone left who needs water?” Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) lifted his hand from the pot, and it was full of water. And people complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) of hunger. He said, “Soon Allah will feed you.” Then we came to the river (i.e., the sea). The sea surged and threw out a creature. We lit a fire on its side and roasted and cooked its meat and ate to our fill. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then I and so-and-so, five men, entered its eye socket, and no one could see us until we came out (the creature was so large). Then we took one of its ribs and called the biggest man in the caravan, who was riding the largest camel with the largest saddle, and he passed under the rib without lowering his head (the rib was so high). Indeed, Allah provides for those who go out in His path."
"1538","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina when the moon split into two pieces. One piece remained on this side of the mountain and the other went to the other side. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Bear witness."""
"1539","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): The people of Makkah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for a sign, so he showed them the splitting of the moon into two parts."
"1540","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` Abu Jahl said, ""Does Muhammad (peace be upon him) put his face on the ground in front of you?"" The people replied, ""Yes."" Abu Jahl said, ""By Lat and Uzza, if I see him in this state (i.e., in prostration), I will trample his neck or smear his face with dust."" Then, when the Prophet (peace be upon him) was praying, he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) with this intention to trample his neck, but the people saw that suddenly Abu Jahl was retreating backwards, shielding himself with his hands from something. The people asked, ""What happened to you?"" He replied, ""I saw between me and Muhammad (peace be upon him) a trench of fire, fear, and wings (those were the wings of angels)."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said, ""If he had come near me, the angels would have torn him limb by limb, part by part."" Then Allah Almighty revealed these verses: ""No! Indeed, man transgresses because he sees himself self-sufficient. Surely to your Lord is the return. Have you seen the one who forbids a servant when he prays? (God forbid, whoever forbids a Muslim from prayer or prevents him from the mosque is like Abu Jahl.) What do you think if he (Muhammad, peace be upon him) is upon guidance or enjoins righteousness? What do you think if he denies and turns away? Does he not know that Allah sees? No! If he does not desist, We will surely drag him by the forelock—a lying, sinful forelock. Then let him call his associates; We will call the angels of punishment. No! Do not obey him."" (Surah Al-‘Alaq: 6-13). In another narration, it is mentioned that he commanded him with what he commanded him. And in another narration, it is mentioned: ""So let him call his people,"" meaning the people of his tribe."
"1541","‘Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) towards Najd for jihad. We found him in a valley where there were many thorny trees. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) dismounted under a tree and hung his sword on a branch, and the people dispersed in the valley seeking shade separately. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said that a man came to me while I was sleeping; he took down the sword, and when I woke up, he was standing over my head. I realized when the naked sword was in his hand. He said, “Who can save you from me now?” I said, “Allah!” Then he said the same thing a second time, and I said, “Allah, the Exalted.” Hearing this, he put the sword back in its sheath. That man is sitting here. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not say anything to him."
"1542","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): A Jewish woman brought poisoned goat meat to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he ate from it. Then the woman was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he asked her, ""What is this that you have done?"" She replied, ""I wanted to kill you."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Allah will not give you the power (to kill His Prophet)."" The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Should we not kill her?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""No."" (This was due to his mercy upon her, and it also shows that he was a true Prophet; otherwise, if he were a king, he would have ordered her to be killed.) The narrator said: I always noticed the effect of that poison on the uvula of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"1543","Sayyiduna Abu Humayd (may Allah be pleased with him) says: In the Battle of Tabuk, we set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). When we reached near a woman's orchard in Wadi al-Qura (a place three miles from Madinah on the way to Syria), the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Estimate how much fruit is in this orchard."" We estimated, and according to the estimate of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), it was found to be ten wasqs. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to the woman: ""Remember this count (estimate) until we return, if Allah wills."" Then we moved on until we reached Tabuk. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tonight a strong wind will blow, so no one should stand up, and whoever has a camel should tie it firmly."" Then it happened as he said: a strong wind blew. A man stood up, and the wind carried him away and threw him between the two mountains of (the valley of) Tay. Ibn al-Ulama, the envoy of the ruler of Aylah, came with a letter and brought a white mule as a gift for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wrote him a reply and sent a sheet as a gift. Then we returned until we reached Wadi al-Qura. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked the woman about the fruit of the orchard: ""How much did it yield?"" She said: ""It yielded exactly ten wasqs."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will go quickly, so whoever among you wishes may go quickly with me, and whoever wishes may stay behind."" We set out until Madinah became visible. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is 'Taba' (Taba is a name of Madinah), and this is Mount Uhud, which loves us and we love it."" Then he said: ""Among the houses of the Ansar, the houses of Banu Najjar are the best (because they were the first to accept Islam), then the houses of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then the houses of Banu Harith bin Khazraj, then the houses of Banu Sa'idah, and there is goodness in all the houses of the Ansar."" Then Sa'd bin Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) met us. Abu Usayd (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Did you not hear that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned the excellence of the houses of the Ansar and put us at the end?"" Hearing this, Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! You mentioned the excellence of the Ansar and put us at the end."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Is it not enough for you that you are among the good ones?"""
"1544","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: My example is like that of a person who lit a fire, and when it illuminated the surroundings, moths and those creatures that fall into the fire began to fall into it, and that person started to prevent them, but they did not stop and kept falling into it. This is the example of me and you: I am holding your backs to keep you away from Hell and saying, ""Stay away from the edge of Hell,"" but you do not listen and keep plunging into it."
"1545","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) granted a concession in a certain matter. When he came to know (that people were not availing it), he stood up to deliver a sermon and said: ""What is the matter with people that they avoid what I have been given a concession in? By Allah, I am the one who knows Allah the most and fears Him the most among you."" (So following me and walking on my path is true piety and righteousness, and unnecessarily burdening oneself and avoiding what is permissible is to doubt its permissibility.)"
"1546","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given a choice between two matters (by Allah Almighty), he would choose the easier one, provided it was not sinful. And if it was sinful, then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would keep farthest from it. And never did he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take revenge for his own sake from anyone, but if someone acted contrary to the command of Allah, then he would punish him."
"1547","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed prayer until his feet became swollen. The people said, ""Why do you endure so much hardship, when all your past and future sins have been forgiven?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""Should I not be a grateful servant of Allah?"""
"1548","'Sayyiduna Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) says that' I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, ""I will be your forerunner at the Hawd (Pond) of Kawthar (that is, I will go ahead and wait for you there and arrange for your drinking)."""
"1549","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: My cistern (Hawd) is equal to the distance of a month's journey, its four corners are equal (that is, its length and width are the same), its water is whiter than silver and its fragrance is better than musk. The cups placed on it are as numerous as the stars in the sky. Whoever drinks from it will never feel thirsty again. Abdullah said that Sayyida Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with her) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I will be at the cistern and I will see who among you comes to me there. And some people will be prevented from coming to me, so I will say: O Lord! These people are from me, from my Ummah. Then it will be said in reply: You do not know what deeds they did after you. By Allah, after you they did not stay for long and turned back on their heels (they turned away from Islam; among them are the Khawarij who separated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and began to consider Muslims as disbelievers, and also those who did not act upon the will of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and troubled and martyred his family—Allah forbid). Ibn Abi Mulaykah (the narrator of the hadith) says: O Allah, we seek Your protection from turning back on our heels or from any tribulation in the religion."
"1550","Narrated from Sayyiduna Haritha bin Wahb (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My cistern is as large as (the distance) from Sana'a to Madinah (a month's journey). Mustawrid said: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) mention the vessels? Haritha said: No. Mustawrid said: There will be vessels there like the stars."
"1551","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""There will be a reservoir before you, the distance between its two banks will be like that between Jarba’ and Adhrah."" In another narration, it is stated: ""My reservoir will be before you."" And in another narration, Ubaydullah says: ""I asked him (i.e., Nafi‘) what are Jarba’ and Adhrah?"" He replied: ""They are two villages in Syria, and the distance between them is that of three nights’ journey."" In another narration, it is stated: ""It is a distance of three days’ journey."""
"1552","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: I will be your forerunner at the Hawd (the Pond), and the distance between its two banks is like that between Sana'a and Aylah, and its drinking vessels are like the stars."
"1553","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What are the vessels of the Hawd (Pond) like?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""By Him in Whose hand is the life of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), the vessels of this Hawd are more numerous than the stars in the sky, and (more than) the dark night without clouds. They are the vessels of Paradise. Whoever drinks from this Hawd will never feel thirsty again (that is, until he enters Paradise). Two streams from Paradise flow into this Hawd. Whoever drinks from it will not feel thirsty, and its length and width are equal, as much as the distance from Aylah to Oman (both are cities in Syria). Its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey."""
"1554","Narrated from Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will be pushing people away from my Hawd (Pond) for the people of Yemen. I will strike with my stick until its water flows towards the people of Yemen. (From this, the great virtue of the people of Yemen is derived. They helped the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, in this world and protected him from enemies, so the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, will also help them in the Hereafter, and they will be the first to drink from the Hawd al-Kawthar.) Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked: What is the width of this Hawd? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Like from here to Oman. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked: What is its water like? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. Two channels pour water into it, which are supplied with water from Paradise; one channel is of gold and the other of silver."
"1555","Narrated from Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one day and offered the funeral prayer for the martyrs of Uhud, then came towards the pulpit and said: I will be your predecessor and a witness over you, and by Allah, I am seeing the Hawd (Pond) of Kawthar at this moment. And I have been given the keys of the treasures of the earth, or the keys of the earth. And by Allah, I do not fear that you will become polytheists after me, but I fear that you will compete with one another for the world and become jealous of one another."
"1556","´Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither very tall nor very short, neither completely white nor completely wheat-colored. The hair of the Prophet (peace be upon him) was neither completely curly nor completely straight. Allah, Glorified and Exalted be He, honored him with Prophethood at the age of forty. Then he (peace be upon him) stayed in Makkah for ten years and in Madinah for ten years, and at the end of his sixtieth year, Allah Almighty took him (peace be upon him) (i.e., he passed away), and at that time there were not even twenty white hairs in his blessed head and beard."
"1557","Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was of medium height and there was a wide gap between his shoulders (i.e., his chest was broad). His hair was thick and reached his earlobes. He (peace and blessings be upon him) used to wear a red garment (i.e., one with red and yellow stripes). I have not seen anyone more beautiful than him (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"1558","Sayyiduna Abu Tufail (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and now, on the earth, there is no one left among those who saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) except me. (The narrator of the hadith, Jariri) says: I asked him, ""You saw him—what was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) like?"" He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was white in complexion, with a tinge of fairness, of medium height, and had a well-proportioned body. Imam Muslim said that Abu Tufail died in the year 100 AH, and among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he was the last to die."
"1559","‘Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that’ the front part of the head and beard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had become white. When he (peace be upon him) applied oil, the whiteness was not visible, and his (peace be upon him) beard was very thick. A person asked, “Was the blessed face of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) long like a sword?” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “No, the blessed face of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was round like the sun and the moon.” And I saw the seal of Prophethood on his (peace be upon him) shoulder, like a pigeon’s egg, and its color matched the color of his body."
"1560","Sayyiduna Sa’ib bin Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) says that my maternal aunt took me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! My nephew is very ill."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) placed his hand on my head and prayed for blessing. Then he performed ablution, and I drank the leftover water from his ablution. Then I stood behind the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and I saw the Seal of Prophethood between his two shoulders, like a raised lump (or like the egg of a partridge, which is a kind of bird)."
"1561","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Sarjis (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ate bread, meat, or tharid with him. (The narrator of the hadith, Asim) says that I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), “Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray for your forgiveness?” He said, “Yes, and for you as well.” Then he recited this verse: “And ask forgiveness for your sin and for the believing men and believing women.” Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that then I went behind him (the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I saw the Seal of Prophethood near his shoulder, at the bone between his two shoulders, it was like a closed fist and on it were moles like warts."
"1562","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had a wide mouth (because for men, a wide mouth is considered good and for women, it is considered undesirable), there were reddish streaks in his eyes, and his heels had little flesh. (Shu’bah) asked Samak, “What is ‘Dali’ al-fam’?” He replied, “A large face.” Then (Shu’bah) asked, “What is ‘Ashkal al-‘ayn’?” He replied, “Eyes with long slits (but Samak’s statement here is incorrect, and the correct meaning is that there was redness mixed in the whiteness).” Shu’bah asked, “What is ‘Manhus al-‘aqibayn’?” He replied, “Heels with little flesh.”"
"1563","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` plucking white hair from the head and beard is disliked, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not use dye. There was some whiteness in his small beard under the lower lip, and some on the temples, and here and there on the head."
"1564","Sayyiduna Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), his complexion was white and he had become old, and Sayyiduna Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) resembled him (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"1565","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was up to his shoulders."
"1566","'Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that' the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was up to half of his ears."
"1567","‘Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that the People of the Book, that is, the Jews and Christians, used to let their hair hang down over their foreheads (that is, they did not part their hair), and the polytheists used to part their hair. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) liked to follow the way of the People of the Book in matters where he had not received any command (that is, compared to the polytheists, the People of the Book were better, so in matters where there was no command, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would adopt the practice of the People of the Book in that matter). So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) also began to let his hair hang over his forehead, and after that, he began to part his hair."
"1568","Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had more modesty than a veiled virgin girl, and whenever he disliked something, we would recognize it from his face."
"1569","'Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that' the blessed complexion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was white and radiant (Nawawi said that this complexion is the best of all complexions), and his blessed sweat was like pearls, and when he walked (the drops of sweat would lean to the right and left, here and there, just as a boat leans), and I have not found even brocade and silk to be as soft as the palm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I have not found in musk and amber the fragrance that was in the blessed body of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1570","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah رضي الله عنه says: I performed the Zuhr prayer with the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم, then he صلى الله عليه وسلم set out to go to his house and I also went out with him صلى الله عليه وسلم. Some children came before us, so the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم passed his hand over the cheek of each child, and he passed his hand over my cheek as well. I felt such coolness and fragrance in his صلى الله عليه وسلم hand as if the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم had taken his hand out from a box of perfume."
"1571","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that revelation would descend upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) even during cold days, and due to the intensity of the revelation, sweat would pour from his forehead."
"1572","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that Harith bin Hisham asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), “How does revelation come to you?” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, “Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell, and that is the hardest for me. Then when it ends, I remember what was said. And sometimes an angel comes to me in the form of a man, and I remember what he says.”"
"1573","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to our house and rested. He began to sweat, and my mother brought a bottle and started wiping his sweat and putting it into it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up and said, ""O Umm Sulaym, what are you doing?"" She replied, ""This is your sweat, which we mix in our perfume, and it is itself the best fragrance of all."""
"1574","‘Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that’ the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to go to the house of Umm Sulaym and would sleep on her bedding, and she would not be at home. One day, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came and was sleeping on her bedding. People called her and said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) is sleeping in your house on your bedding. Hearing this, she came and saw that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was sweating, and his sweat had collected on the leather bedding. Umm Sulaym opened her box and began to wipe the sweat and collect it in bottles. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) woke up startled and said, “O Umm Sulaym! What are you doing?” She said, “O Messenger of Allah! We hope for blessings for our children from this.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “You have done right.”"
"1575","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the morning prayer, the servants of Madinah would bring their vessels of water, and whichever vessel was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he would dip his hand into it. And sometimes, even on cold days, it would happen that he would dip his hand."
"1576","´Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) while the barber was shaving his head and the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) were around him; they wanted that not a single hair should fall to the ground, but rather fall into someone's hand."
"1577","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that a woman had a slight mental disorder. She said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I have something to ask you (meaning, I want to say something that I cannot say in front of people)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""O Umm Fulan! (i.e., he mentioned her name) I will do your work wherever you wish."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went aside with her on the road until she finished what she wanted to say."
"1578","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I have not seen anyone show as much affection to children as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did. The son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), Sayyiduna Ibrahim, used to be nursed (in the outskirts of Madinah). (The outskirts were some villages near Madinah.) The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to go there, and we would go with him. Then he would visit the house, where there would be smoke because the husband of ""Annah"" was a blacksmith. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would take the child, love him, and then return. Amr said: When Sayyiduna Ibrahim passed away, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ibrahim is my son. He passed away while still nursing. Now he has two wet nurses who will nurse him in Paradise for the duration he was to be nursed."""
"1579","Narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that Aqra’ bin Habis saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him). He said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I have ten children and I have not kissed any of them."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Whoever does not show mercy (to children, orphans, the helpless, and the weak), Allah will not show mercy to him."""
"1580","´Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was on a journey and an Abyssinian slave whose name was Anjasha was singing a song. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""O Anjasha! Drive slowly and lead the camels as if they are carrying glass vessels."""
"1581","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was the most beautiful of all people, the most generous of all, and the bravest of all. One night, the people of Madinah were frightened (by the fear of an enemy's arrival), so they headed towards the direction from where the sound was coming. On the way, they found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) returning (he had gone ahead of everyone alone to investigate), and he was the first to go towards the sound. He was riding bareback on the horse of Sayyiduna Abu Talhah, and there was a sword hanging around his neck. He was saying, ""Do not fear, do not fear. This horse is like a river (swift),"" and previously that horse was slow (this too was a miracle of the Prophet, that it became swift)."
"1582","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the best in character among all people. One day, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told me to go for an errand, so I said, ""By Allah, I will not go,"" but in my heart, I intended to go for the task he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had ordered. (According to the habit of childhood, I outwardly refused.) Eventually, I went out until I met some boys who were playing in the market (probably I started watching them, and thus got delayed in the task). Suddenly, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from behind and held me by the neck. I looked towards him and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was smiling. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""O Unais!"" (This is a diminutive form of Anas, said affectionately by the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), ""Did you go where I told you to go?"" I said, ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah! I am going."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""By Allah, I served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for nine years, and I do not remember that for any task which I did, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Why did you do this?' or for any task which I did not do, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Why did you not do it?'"""
"1583","‘Sayyiduna Urwah bin Zubair says that’ Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to narrate and say, “Listen, O lady of the chamber! Listen, O lady of the chamber!” And Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) was performing prayer. When she finished the prayer, she said to Urwah, “Did you hear Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) and how many narrations he related in that time? And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to speak in such a manner that if someone wanted to count (his words), he could count them (i.e., he spoke slowly and clearly, and this is the proper etiquette. Speaking hastily and rapidly is not the way of wisdom and intelligence).”"
"1584","Shafiq bin Abu Wa'il says that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them) used to give us admonition every Thursday. A person said, ""O Abu Abdur Rahman!"" (this is the kunyah of Sayyiduna Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him), ""we wish to listen to your talk and we like it. We wish that you narrate hadith to us every day."" Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""The reason I do not narrate hadith to you every day is that I dislike putting you into boredom, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to choose a specific day among several days for us, because he disliked causing us distress (i.e., being burdensome)."""
"1585","‘Abdullah ibn ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was the most generous of all people in giving wealth, and his generosity was greatest in the month of Ramadan. And Jibril (peace be upon him) used to meet him every year in Ramadan until the end of the month. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would recite the Qur’an to him. When Jibril (peace be upon him) met him, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was more generous in giving wealth than the blowing wind. (It is understood from this that one should be more generous in a blessed month and at a blessed time.)"
"1586","Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that it never happened that anything was asked from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said no."
"1587","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for the sheep between the two mountains, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave them to him. He went back to his people and said, ""O people! Accept Islam, for by Allah, Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) gives gifts without any fear of poverty."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said that a person would become Muslim only for worldly gain, then he would become such a Muslim that Islam would become dearer to him than the whole world. (At first he became Muslim out of greed, but later he became sincere.)"
"1588","Narrated from Ibn Shihab, he states that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fought in the battle of the conquest of Makkah. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) set out with the Muslims and fought in Hunayn, so Allah Almighty granted victory to His religion and to the Muslims. On that day, he (peace and blessings be upon him) gave Safwan bin Umayyah one hundred camels (from the spoils of war). Then he gave him another one hundred camels. Then he gave him another one hundred camels. Ibn Shihab says that Sa'id bin Musayyib narrated to me that Safwan said: By Allah, whatever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave me, he gave me, and (before that) in my eyes he was the most disliked of all people. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) continued to give me until he became the most beloved of all people to me."
"1589","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the wealth of Bahrain comes to us, I will give you this much, this much, and this much, and he indicated with both his hands (i.e., three handfuls). Then, before the wealth of Bahrain arrived, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away. That wealth came to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He ordered a caller to announce that whoever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had promised something to, or whoever had a debt upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), should come. Hearing this, I stood up and said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had promised me that if the wealth of Bahrain came, he would give me this much, this much, and this much. Hearing this, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) gave me a handful and then said to me, ""Count it."" I counted it, and it was five hundred. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Take double of it as well"" (so it became three handfuls)."
"1590","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jubair bin Mut’im (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I have several names; I am Muhammad, Ahmad, and Al-Mahi, meaning that through me Allah will erase disbelief. And I am Al-Hashir, people will be gathered to me on the Day of Resurrection for intercession. And I am Al-‘Aqib, meaning there will be no prophet after me. And Allah Almighty has named you (peace and blessings be upon him) Ra’uf and Rahim (very gentle and very merciful) (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"1591","Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to mention several names of himself to us, and he (peace be upon him) said: I am Muhammad (peace be upon him), and Ahmad, and Muqaffi (that is, Aqib), and Hashir, and the Prophet of Repentance, and the Prophet of Mercy (because repentance and mercy have been brought by him, peace be upon him)."
"1592","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stayed in Makkah for thirteen years during which revelation would come to him, and he stayed in Madinah for ten years. And he passed away at the age of sixty-three years."
"1593","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to hear the voice (of angels) in Makkah for fifteen years and see the light (of angels or Allah’s verses) for seven years, but did not see any form. Then for eight years, revelation used to come, and he stayed in Madinah for ten years. (This narration is rare.)"
"1594","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away at the age of sixty-three years, and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) also passed away at the age of sixty-three years, and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) also passed away at the age of sixty-three years."
"1595","‘Ammar, the freed slave of Banu Hashim, says: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), “How old was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when he passed away?” He said, “I did not think that you, being from his people, would not know this.” I said, “I asked people, but they differed in this matter, so I thought it better to hear your statement about it.” Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, “Do you know how to calculate?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Remember forty years, for at that age he (peace and blessings be upon him) became a Prophet. Now add fifteen, for the time he (peace and blessings be upon him) stayed in Makkah, sometimes in safety and sometimes in fear. Now add ten more, which passed after the migration to Madinah (so altogether it becomes sixty-five years). And before this, the hadith of Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) has passed that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away at the age of sixty years. (See Hadith: 1556).”"
"1596","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: Indeed, when Allah the Exalted shows mercy to a nation, He causes its prophet to pass away before the destruction of that nation, and the prophet becomes a forerunner for his nation. And when He wills the destruction of a nation, He destroys it before the prophet, and by their destruction, He cools the eyes of the prophet, because that nation denies him and disobeys his commands."
"1597","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him): A man from the Ansar had a dispute with Sayyiduna Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him), who was the cousin of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) through his paternal aunt, before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding the water at Harrah (Harrah refers to land with black stones), from which they used to water the date-palm trees. The Ansari said, ""Let the water flow so that it reaches (my land)."" Sayyiduna Zubair refused. Eventually, they both brought their dispute before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Zubair, ""O Zubair! Water (your trees) first, then let the water flow to your neighbor."" Upon hearing this, the Ansari became angry and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Zubair is your cousin through your aunt (that is why you have favored him)."" Upon hearing this, the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) changed color, and he said, ""O Zubair! Water (your trees) and then withhold the water until it reaches the embankments."" Sayyiduna Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""By Allah, I think this verse was revealed about this matter: 'But no, by your Lord, they will not (truly) believe until they make you judge in their disputes, then find in themselves no discomfort from what you have judged and submit in (full, willing) submission.' ((Complete verse: ... la yu’minuna hatta yuhakkimuka ...))"""
"1598","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard something from his companions (which was bad), so he delivered a sermon and said: Paradise and Hell were brought before me, and I have never seen such goodness and such evil as I have seen today (meaning the blessings in Paradise and the punishment in Hell). If you knew what I know, you would surely laugh little and weep much. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said that no day was harder on the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than that day. They covered their heads and the sound of weeping began to come from them. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and said: We are pleased with Allah as our Lord, with Islam as our religion, and with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as our Prophet. A man stood up and said: Who was my father? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your father was so-and-so (and mentioned his name). Then this verse was revealed: ""O you who believe! Do not ask about things which, if made plain to you, may cause you trouble."""
"1599","`Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The greatest sin among the Muslims is that of the Muslim who asked about something which was not forbidden to the Muslims, but due to his questioning, it became forbidden."
"1600","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Where is my father?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""In Hell."" When he turned away, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called him back and said, ""My father and your father are both in Hell."""
"1601","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him), he states that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""Whatever I forbid you from, abstain from it, and whatever I command you to do, do it to the best of your ability. Indeed, those before you were only destroyed because of their excessive questioning and their disagreement with their prophets."""
"1602","Sayyiduna Talhah bin Ubaidullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I passed by some people with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who were near date-palm trees. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, ""What are these people doing?"" The people replied, ""They are grafting, that is, they place the male with the female so that it becomes fruitful (i.e., bears more fruit)."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""I do not think there is any benefit in this."" When this news reached those people, they stopped grafting. Afterwards, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of this, he said, ""If there is benefit for them in it, then let them do it. I had only expressed an opinion, so do not take my opinion. But when I state a command from Allah Almighty, then act upon it, for I do not lie against Allah Almighty."""
"1603","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: By Him in Whose hand is the life of Muhammad, a time will come when you will not be able to see me, and seeing me will be dearer to you than your children and your wealth. (Therefore, consider my company a blessing, life is uncertain, and learn matters of religion quickly.) Abu Ishaq (i.e., Ibn Muhammad bin Sufyan) said: In my view, the meaning of this is that ""for them to see me"" means that seeing the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) will be given precedence. And in this statement, there is advancement and delay (i.e., the order of the words is changed)."
"1604","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among my Ummah, the most loving towards me will be those people who will be born after me; one of them would wish that he could sacrifice his family and wealth just to see me."
